    <div class="frame">
      <div class="cat-head">
        <span class="cat-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
        </span>
        <div class="cat-text">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="num">48</span>Track B recap</p>
          <h2 class="h2">What the API track taught us.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="frame-body">
      <ul class="checklist" style="margin-top: 28px; font-size: 22px; gap: 16px;">
        <li>Cache stable prefixes: system prompts and examples reused across calls drop input cost by up to 90%.</li>
        <li>Batch and flex non-urgent work: the Batch API cuts cost 50% for anything that tolerates a delay.</li>
        <li>Route by task: small or deterministic tasks go to a cheaper model; heavy reasoning goes to a larger one.</li>
        <li>Tune effort before switching models: try a lower thinking budget first; the gain is often enough.</li>
        <li>Cap output: structured output and <code>max_tokens</code> prevent runaway generation that costs 3 to 6 times input.</li>
        <li>Measure cost per outcome: cost per merged PR or resolved issue, not cost per token.</li>
        <li>Allocate to a user: tag every call with user and feature metadata so you know who incurs the cost.</li>
        <li>Set a hard brake: <code>max_turns</code> and <code>max_budget_usd</code> in code, plus a workspace spend limit in the Console.</li>
      </ul>      </div>
    </div>
